Pre-base-date pre-registration revision per K4 amendment pattern.
Closes V1 from Day 75 prelaunch unknowns report.

New peer section 'Silent-FALLBACK exclusion (locked)' between §5(6) eligibility
rulings and Confidence-level policy. Three subsections:

Rule: provider mappings appearing in static FALLBACK_MODELS arrays of catalog-gated
adapters (cerebras, fireworks, groq, hyperbolic) without live-catalog confirmation
are excluded from the inaugural eligibility universe. Rule scopes to catalog-gated
adapters only; static-by-design and api_inline_price adapter classes are out of
scope.

Operationalization: omission applied at worksheet-generation layer via
tools/coverage_check.py --registry-state 0013 --verbose; rebalancing-cadence
re-verification with exit-from-FALLBACK_MODELS pathway to re-eligibility.

Disclosure: per-day exclusions published in vipi_audit_records.audit_json.silent_fallback_exclusions,
parallel to outlier_exclusions shape per methodology §10.4. Methodology §11.3
already references this disclosure key.

Operational anchor: migration 0008 header L84-L91 documents the rule application
at Day 73 coverage_check run; this commit codifies that operational anchor as
locked curation policy.
